<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan vehicle exports surge 33.9% yr/yr--JAMA.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan vehicle exports surge 33.9% yr/yr--JAMA.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vehicle exports rose 33.9 percent in January from a year earlier to 355,190 units, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers' Association (JAMA) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It was the eighth successive month in which exports had risen on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>		     JANUARY	  YR/YR CHANGE</p>
<p> Cars		280,046	    +35.1</p>
<p> Trucks	     71,024	    +29.5</p>
<p> Buses		 4,120	    +27.5</p>
<p>Exports by destination:</p>
<p> Asia		 40,706	     -9.4</p>
<p> Mideast	    27,510	    +43.2</p>
<p> Europe	     96,349	    +22.6</p>
<p> - EU		 81,508	    +19.1</p>
<p> North America   132,691	    +69.5</p>
<p> - U.S.	    124,834	    +75.3</p>
<p> Latin America    24,762	    +30.0</p>
<p> Africa	     11,789	    +35.0</p>
<p> Oceania	    20,306	    +28.2</p>
<p> Other		 1,077	    +68.0</p>
<p>Exports by five major manufacturers:</p>
<p> Toyota	132,191	+71.1</p>
<p> Nissan	 53,123	+11.8</p>
<p> Mazda	  43,233	+26.9</p>
<p> Honda	  40,792	+34.5</p>
<p> Mitsubishi   38,252	 +6.9</p>
</text>
